WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.703 --> 00:00:06.139
In this lesson, we do an infill on a set that has been on for a few weeks,

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:06.910
step by step.

00:00:07.363 --> 00:00:11.056
The nails have grown out, there is a strip of new nail at the cuticle,

00:00:11.006 --> 00:00:12.670
and the apex has moved forward.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.870
The method is the same for builder gel and acrylic.

00:00:16.045 --> 00:00:17.870
Where they differ, I will say so.

00:00:18.299 --> 00:00:20.110
Keep in mind three things throughout:

00:00:20.262 --> 00:00:24.494
never infill over lifting, never file the natural nail or the skin,

00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:26.990
and rebuild the apex in the right place.

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:28.274
Step one:

00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:29.954
consultation and check.

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:33.634
Wash and sanitize your hands, and the hands of the client.

00:00:34.142 --> 00:00:35.074
Ask the client:

00:00:35.423 --> 00:00:39.554
in the past few weeks, has any nail broken, lifted, or hurt?

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:44.354
Then look closely at each nail in good light, tilting the finger back and forth.

00:00:44.702 --> 00:00:48.834
Small lifting is often just a faint line at the edge, very easy to miss.

00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:53.916
If it has lifted in large patches, with air pockets or discoloration,

00:00:53.866 --> 00:00:56.754
or the nail hurts, or is red and swollen,

00:00:57.106 --> 00:00:58.514
do not do an infill.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.714
Remove it all, or advise the client to see a doctor.

00:01:02.213 --> 00:01:06.173
If certain nails often lift or break, note it in the client record,

00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:08.274
so next time you know how to adjust.

00:01:08.841 --> 00:01:09.634
Step two:

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.794
prep the new growth like a new nail, as in the gel polish lesson.

00:01:14.213 --> 00:01:15.954
Dry prep, no soaking.

00:01:16.463 --> 00:01:21.474
Push back the cuticle gently, removing the thin layer of skin stuck to the new nail.

00:01:22.058 --> 00:01:26.834
Then glide a buffer very lightly, only over the new growth, to remove the shine.

00:01:27.193 --> 00:01:28.594
Do not thin the nail.

00:01:29.218 --> 00:01:30.041
Step three:

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:31.321
deal with the lifting.

00:01:31.653 --> 00:01:35.001
Find the edge of the product at the cuticle and along both sides.

00:01:35.346 --> 00:01:38.941
Wherever it has lifted, file gently until the lifting is gone,

00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:42.601
and the remaining edge is firmly bonded and flush with the nail.

00:01:42.962 --> 00:01:45.881
When you are done, look again carefully under the lamp.

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:49.561
If the edge still shows a faint white line, it is still lifted.

00:01:49.764 --> 00:01:52.540
Do not pry, and do not pull the lifted part off,

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.721
because it will take layers of the natural nail with it.

00:01:56.213 --> 00:02:00.681
If you keep filing and it is still lifted, lifted in a large patch, stop.

00:02:01.188 --> 00:02:05.801
This set needs to be removed completely and redone, as in the gel removal lesson.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.405
Step four:

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:09.005
thin the old layer.

00:02:09.747 --> 00:02:13.328
Lay the file flat on the nail, and file away some of the thickness,

00:02:13.278 --> 00:02:15.805
especially the old apex that has moved forward.

00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:19.283
If the nails are too long, cut and file them shorter,

00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:21.165
keeping the shape the client chose.

00:02:21.685 --> 00:02:24.927
The goal is an old layer that is evenly thin and neat,

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:27.645
so the new layer has room to rebuild the apex.

00:02:28.061 --> 00:02:31.005
Do not file through the old layer down to the natural nail.

00:02:31.177 --> 00:02:35.645
If you use an electric file, only do so once you have been properly trained:

00:02:35.913 --> 00:02:38.745
a moderate speed, the bit always on the product,

00:02:38.695 --> 00:02:41.005
and never near the cuticle or the skin.

00:02:41.675 --> 00:02:42.624
Step five:

00:02:42.846 --> 00:02:43.904
blend the seam.

00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:48.144
Where the old layer meets the new growth, there is usually a small step.

00:02:48.677 --> 00:02:53.093
File gently until the step thins out, flat and flush with the new nail,

00:02:53.043 --> 00:02:55.184
so you can no longer feel a ridge.

00:02:55.605 --> 00:03:00.224
File flat, with a light hand, and keep the file away from the skin at the cuticle.

00:03:00.874 --> 00:03:01.830
Step six:

00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:02.630
cleanse.

00:03:02.852 --> 00:03:04.310
The extraction is still running.

00:03:04.738 --> 00:03:05.990
Brush away all the dust;

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:07.030
do not blow.

00:03:07.458 --> 00:03:10.870
Then wipe the whole nail with a lint free wipe and nail cleanser.

00:03:11.135 --> 00:03:13.750
From now on, do not touch the nail surface.

00:03:14.395 --> 00:03:15.208
Step seven:

00:03:15.548 --> 00:03:16.488
the bonding layer.

00:03:16.757 --> 00:03:20.408
Apply it only to the new growth, and leave a fine line from the skin.

00:03:20.841 --> 00:03:24.408
Do not brush it over the old layer, unless the brand says so.

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:28.248
For gel, that is the base or the bonder of the brand.

00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:31.128
Whether to cure it or not follows the instructions.

00:03:31.422 --> 00:03:36.408
For acrylic, it is primer, dabbed on very thinly, only on the natural nail.

00:03:37.079 --> 00:03:38.902
Step eight, with builder gel.

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.548
A very thin layer over the whole nail,

00:03:41.498 --> 00:03:44.198
like the base layer in the builder gel lesson,

00:03:44.148 --> 00:03:46.502
so the new gel joins with the old layer.

00:03:46.845 --> 00:03:49.222
Then place a bead of gel in the middle of the nail.

00:03:49.564 --> 00:03:52.965
Gently guide it towards the cuticle, thinner and thinner,

00:03:52.915 --> 00:03:56.022
stopping with a gap as thin as a hair from the skin.

00:03:56.449 --> 00:03:58.502
Then out to the sides, and to the tip.

00:03:58.748 --> 00:04:01.539
Turn the finger upside down for a few seconds,

00:04:01.489 --> 00:04:04.102
so the gel gathers by itself into the apex,

00:04:04.289 --> 00:04:05.142
in the right place.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:09.062
Turn it back to check, then cure for the full time the brand recommends.

00:04:09.586 --> 00:04:13.234
If the client feels heat, let her take the hand out for a few seconds,

00:04:13.184 --> 00:04:14.982
then cure again for the full time.

00:04:15.609 --> 00:04:17.544
With acrylic, it is a little different.

00:04:18.018 --> 00:04:21.862
The first bead is small, a little wetter, placed on the new growth,

00:04:21.812 --> 00:04:22.824
near the cuticle.

00:04:23.379 --> 00:04:28.264
Stroke it very thin, thinner towards the skin, and never let it touch the skin.

00:04:28.738 --> 00:04:32.344
If it does, flick it away right away while it is still soft.

00:04:32.775 --> 00:04:34.904
Then another bead goes on the stress area.

00:04:35.328 --> 00:04:40.024
Press lightly, stroke it so it blends with the old layer, and rebuild the apex.

00:04:40.255 --> 00:04:43.384
Wait for the acrylic to harden, for the time the brand gives.

00:04:43.635 --> 00:04:45.224
Tap the brush handle lightly:

00:04:45.325 --> 00:04:47.944
a dry, clear click means it is ready.

00:04:48.535 --> 00:04:49.398
Step nine:

00:04:49.578 --> 00:04:50.838
finishing with the file.

00:04:51.318 --> 00:04:54.518
File the surface smooth, keeping the apex you just built.

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:57.478
Neaten the side walls, and even out the tip.

00:04:57.723 --> 00:05:02.457
At the cuticle, where the new layer thins out, blend it into the natural nail,

00:05:02.407 --> 00:05:04.438
but do not file the natural nail,

00:05:04.469 --> 00:05:05.958
and do not touch the skin.

00:05:06.295 --> 00:05:08.358
Brush off the dust, and cleanse.

00:05:08.797 --> 00:05:12.198
Then look again from above, from the side, and from the tip.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.038
The nails must all match:

00:05:14.274 --> 00:05:18.998
thin at the cuticle, moderately high over the stress area, and thin at the tip.

00:05:19.171 --> 00:05:20.358
Just like on the first day.

00:05:21.056 --> 00:05:21.954
Step ten:

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.154
color and top coat, as in the gel polish lesson.

00:05:25.577 --> 00:05:29.394
Thin coats, capping the free edge, and cure for the full time.

00:05:29.906 --> 00:05:34.434
Then put a drop of cuticle oil on the skin around the nails, and massage gently.

00:05:34.757 --> 00:05:37.234
Before the client leaves, book the next infill:

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:41.394
about three to four weeks for gel, and about two to three weeks for acrylic.

00:05:41.663 --> 00:05:42.514
And tell the client:

00:05:42.853 --> 00:05:45.954
if it lifts, do not pry it or peel it yourself;

00:05:46.191 --> 00:05:47.714
come back to the salon early.

00:05:48.331 --> 00:05:49.710
Once the client has gone:

00:05:49.841 --> 00:05:53.470
used files, buffers and cotton go in a bin with a lid.

00:05:53.803 --> 00:05:56.349
Metal tools go to be cleaned and sterilized.

00:05:56.618 --> 00:05:59.230
Close the gel bottles and the acrylic dish tightly.

00:05:59.656 --> 00:06:02.350
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
